# Simulation of Multi-State Processes with Controlled Markov Deviation
# Based on Method S6: BIC-based Markov Memory Index (MMI)
# ============================================================================

# The following code implements only the state-outcome data-generating
# mechanism used in the MMI sensitivity analysis. It generates wide_data
# under different nominal higher-order Markov settings using
# simulate_mmi_scenario().
#
# This section does not repeat the complete 500-replicate BCMC fitting and
# performance-evaluation code because those steps are identical to the main
# simulation analysis.
#
# For the complete MMI sensitivity analysis, within each of the 500
# simulation replicates, replace the original state-outcome generation block
# in run_one_sim() with a call to:
#
# wide_data <- simulate_mmi_scenario(
#   psi = psi,
#   phi = phi,
#   n_patients = n_patients,
