# wide_data <- as.data.frame(wide_data)
#
# After wide_data has been generated, the remaining steps are unchanged:
# 1. select the required observation-time columns;
# 2. convert wide_data into transition-specific survival data;
# 3. refit BCMC and the comparator models;
# 4. select the post-estimation smoothing model using ZBIC;
# 5. calculate bias, MAE, MSE, sMAPE, interval coverage, and interval width.
#
# The nominal generating order psi is a simulation setting and should not
# automatically be interpreted as the realized MMI. The realized MMI should
# be estimated and validated for each generated dataset using compute_mmi().
#
# Thus, the code below demonstrates the MMI-specific data-generation step,
